1.0.4-snapshot
  Added: Perception trace, its own tab and log file, one switch per system. Hearing: every event that reaches a nearby stalker or mutant with its power against his threshold.
    Vision: when he starts or stops seeing you and his detection progress. Memory: his visual, sound and hit memory of you.
    Danger: his held danger, the action answering it down to the leaf (take cover, look out, hold, detour, search), and his reaction with the distance he moved.
    Enemy: his enemy pick and drop, with whether he heard or saw you first. It reads engine state only. A run with an AI mod on and a run with it off compare line for line.
  Added: Reset to defaults button on the Development tab, and the Immediate flush switch now covers the perception log.
  Fixed: rare arena census crash when the engine recycles a dead combatant's id to another object
  Added: timed event scheduling works correctly with major modpacks (globals resolve at call time for demonized_time_events compatibility)
  Added: version displayed at startup (mod + xlibs)
  Changed: MCM visual refresh
  Compatibility:
    Requires themrdemonized modded exes 20250908+ or AOEngine v0.55+.

  Performance and Infrastructure
    - Rebuilt the validator into layered rules for crashes, unsafe engine usage, performance, best practices, smoke load, and secret leaks.
    - The validator runs on every change, locally and in CI, and a grade gate fails the build on any finding.
    - Profiled and tuned with JitProfiler, an engine-native, scientific profiler.
    - Consolidated the whole engine layer into xlibs and standardized naming and structure across every mod.

